# Mossadegh

We are delighted to learn that Mossadegh, the venerable former Prime Minister of Iran, will be released from prison this Sunday.

Mossadegh is said to be eighty years old. Having endured three years of rigorous imprisonment, he will be released on Sunday.

This elderly man of fearless heart was the one who nationalised Iran's Abadan oil industry, which had been under British domination.

That event became the precedent for the position Nasser is taking today over the Suez issue.

Britain sent warships. Several world powers issued threats. The old man did not waver.

Even opposition from the Shah of Iran arose; he paid it no heed.

They summoned him before the international court. Mossadegh appeared in person, argued the case, and won.

But imperialism employed many intrigues to destroy his influence.

The Shah, who had fled the country, returned with renewed strength.

Opposition to Mossadegh was stirred up.

They said he would be sent to the gallows. In the end, the Shah sentenced him to three years.

It was then said that Mossadegh might be deported after his release.

The world will not accept cruelty going to such lengths.

It would be just to allow Mossadegh, whose heart can bear anything, to live in his homeland and offer it the benefit of his great passion and profound wisdom.

We rejoice at the release of the venerable Mossadegh.

(*Dravida Nadu*, news item, 2-8-26)
